+# Diffusers Production Hardening Runbook (summary)
+
+This runbook summarizes the practical steps to harden the Diffusers stack for production.
+
+1) Replace in-memory queue with Redis+Celery
+ - Deploy Redis (helm/diffusers-chart/templates/redis-deployment.yaml)
+ - Deploy Celery workers using Dockerfile.worker
+ - Use server_celery.py to enqueue tasks and poll results
+
+2) Autoscaling
+ - Use KEDA with Redis list trigger (helm/diffusers-chart/templates/keda-scaledobject-redis.yaml)
+ - Instrument queue length metrics and GPU utilization
+
+3) Performance
+ - Enable xformers and memory-efficient attention in worker images
+ - Use mixed precision (fp16) on GPUs
+ - Consider offloading/atten-slicing and scheduler tuning
+
+4) Moderation & Safety
+ - Replace blocklist with ML classifiers (services/serving/diffusers/moderation_ml.py)
+ - Add human escalation (services/serving/diffusers/human_escalation.py) for blocked outputs
+ - Run CI moderation tests (.github/workflows/moderation_ci.yml)
